          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "# Museum Ticket Generator\n# Prices: under 5 free, under 18 pays $8, 65 and up pays $10, everyone else $15\n\nage = int(input(\"How old is the visitor? \"))",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "museum_ticket_plan.txt",
          "contents": "*** MY PLAN: ***\n\nStarting price (Rule 1): $____\n\nRule 2\nQuestion about age, in words: ____________________________?\nCondition, in Python: ____________________\nIf True, price becomes: $____\n\nRule 3\nQuestion about age, in words: ____________________________?\nCondition, in Python: ____________________\nIf True, price becomes: $____\n\nRule 4\nQuestion about age, in words: ____________________________?\nCondition, in Python: ____________________\nIf True, price becomes: $____\n\nWhich rule goes last, and why?\n\n\n*** MY TESTING: ***\n\nPredict the price for each age BEFORE you run your program. Then run it and record what it printed.\n\nAge | Rules that apply | Predicted price | Actual price\n----|------------------|-----------------|-------------\n3   |                  |                 |\n5   |                  |                 |\n12  |                  |                 |\n18  |                  |                 |\n40  |                  |                 |\n65  |                  |                 |\n70  |                  |                 |\n\n\n*** MY DOCUMENTATION CHECK: ***\n\nMy partner read only my comments and predicted the price for age ___ and age ___.\nWere they right? ________\nIf not, what did I change in my comments?\n\n\n*** MY REFLECTION: ***\n\nIf you used AI Tutor to help, reflect below on how you used it and how you used its output.\n\n\nHow did testing go? Did you update any part of your program as a result? Explain.",
